Time-phased KPI trend (the easy way): bind a single time field (Month, Quarter, Year) under the Period role. The visual auto-aggregates rows back to one per project AND draws each KPI tile's sparkline grouped by Period — no per-period measures needed.
Manual KPI trend: open the ⚙ on a KPI tile and tick measures as trend points. Each ticked measure becomes one point on the sparkline, in tick order.
Column rendering: click the ⚙ on any column header to pick its render type — number, money, percent, progress bar, bullet chart, variance, status pill, date, sparkline or box plot.
Project features: Timeline, Ask, the decision insights and Focus read the rows as projects. Using the grid for something else? Format pane -> Grid -> Project Features = Off turns the whole layer off and leaves a plain table.
Excel: the Excel button exports what you see — filters, Focus, question and hidden columns included. The hierarchy arrives as collapsible outline groups, totals and subtotals as live SUBTOTAL formulas, calculated columns as live formulas. Power BI asks you to confirm the download; your admin can switch downloads from custom visuals off.
Status bar: drag over cells, as in Excel — the bar at the bottom shows Sum, Average, Count, Min and Max of the selection (Average only for percentages). Ctrl+C copies the selected cells; Esc clears.
Tabs: the sheet tabs at the bottom switch between ready-made layouts — Overview, Financial, Schedule, Health, Steering — built from the columns you bound, followed by your saved views; + saves the current layout. Right-click a column header to sort, filter, group by, hide or configure it; hidden columns come back with Show all columns or the Overview tab.
Ask: the question chips under the legend — What is late? Who is over budget? Where is the money? — answer from the data in view. The number on a chip is how many projects answer it (✓ = none). Click one: the grid keeps those projects, worst first, tints the columns the answer comes from and spells the answer out. Click again to clear.
Focus: the Focus button keeps only the projects that need attention — late, behind schedule, over budget, stalled or flagged at risk — opens every level down to them and adds a Why column with the reason per project. Totals and tiles follow. Click again to see everything.
Timeline: with a start and a finish date among the Columns, a Timeline column draws a bar per row on one shared date scale — solid fill = % done, red stripes = should be done by today but is not, red line = past the finish, dashed line = today. ⚙ on its header picks the fields; Format pane → Grid → Show Timeline Column hides it.
Calculated columns: the Calc button adds a column computed from two numeric columns — A − B, A + B, A ÷ B, A as % of B or % difference. Totals apply the calculation to the totals of A and B.
Status dot: comes from the Status column; tones are derived from the status vocabulary (On Track, At Risk, Off Track, etc.).
Grouping: ⚙ on a column → 'Group rows by this column' to fold rows into headers + subtotal rows.
